N2  -  INTERVENTION: Trial is evaluating Robotic surgery for resection of their early‐stage lung cancer. Surgery will be performed by a qualified thoracic surgeon and the surgery will take up to 3 hours. This is a standard of care treatment of lung cancer currently via keyhole surgery where the surgeon operates the instruments robotically. The trial will be evaluating the short‐term outcomes post‐surgery (compared to VATS [Video‐Assisted Thoracic Surgery] resection) such as length of surgery, complications, length of post operative hospitalisation, and will also evaluate quality of life post‐surgery. CONDITION: Cancer ‐ Lung ‐ Non small cell Lung Cancer; ; Lung Cancer PRIMARY OUTCOME: The trial is intended to determine the difference in participant‐reported HRQOL outcomes between RTS‐Lobectomy and VATS‐Lobectomy at 12 weeks. [Health related Quality of Life (HRQOL). 12 weeks post surgery.] SECONDARY OUTCOME: 5‐year survival rate[Survival data via patient follow‐up 5 years post surgery.] Amount of intraoperative blood loss with RTS‐Lobectomy.[Calculation of total blood loss of VATS‐Lobectomy will be compared with RTS‐Lobectomy At completion of surgery.] Determination of higher quality pathological staging by improved lymphadenectomy. [Anatomical pathological assessment Time of surgery.] Difference in quality of life between the treatment groups, as measured by which coincide with standard of care intervals of oncological surveillance.[The Health‐Related Quality of Life questionnaire Weeks 3 and 7 and 12; months 6, 12, 18, 24; and years 3, 4, and 5, ] Duration of hospital stay[Patient surgery till discharge date Hospitalisation] Duration of surgery between RTS‐ Lobectomy vs VATS‐ Lobectomy[Duration of surgery between RTS‐ Lobectomy vs VATS‐ Lobectomy will be compared. At completion of surgery] Length of chest tube drainage required[Days of chest tube drainage required Hospital stay] Post‐operative analgesia requirements between RTS‐Lobectomy vs VATS‐Lobectomy.[The analgesia requirements between RTS‐Lobectomy vs VATS‐Lobectomy will be compared. During the duration of stay in hospital and post discharge. ] INCLUSION CRITERIA: • Age 18 years and above • Clinical stage I, II or IIIa non‐small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) • Candidates for minimally invasive pulmonary surgery, as determined by the operating surgeon.
